ic lymphoma; Enrylaze to treat acute lymphoblastic leukemia and lymphoblastic lymphoma; Zepzelca for the treatment of metastatic small cell lung cancer with disease progression on or after platinum-based chemotherapy; Ziihera to treat HER2-positive biliary tract cancers; Modeyso for the treatment of diffuse midline glioma harboring an H3 K27M mutation; and Defitelio to treat severe veno-occlusive disease. It also develops Zanidatamab in Phase 3 trial to treat HER2-positive gastroesophageal adenocarcinoma (GEA) and biliary tract cancers (BTC); Dordaviprone to treat H3 K27M-mutant diffuse glioma; and Vyxeos for the treatment of newly-diagnosed therapy-related acute myeloid leukemia. In addition, the company is developing Zanidatamab to treat neoadjuvant and adjuvant breast cancer; Vyxeos for the treatment of High-risk MDS, newly diagnosed untreated patients with high-risk AML, and De novo intermediate or adverse risk AML stratified by genomics; and JZP3507 to treat pheochromocytoma and paraganglioma that are in Phase 2 clinical trials. Further, it develops JZP815 to treat Raf and Ras mutant tumors; JZP898 for the IFN INDUKIN molecule in solid tumors; and JZP047 to treat absence epilepsy that are in Phase 1 clinical trials. The company collaboration agreements with Redx Pharma plc, Autifony Therapeutics Limited, Zymeworks Inc., Sumitomo Pharma Co., Ltd., Werewolf Therapeutics, Inc; and AbCellera Biologics Inc. Jazz Pharmaceuticals plc was founded in 2003 and is headquartered in Dublin, Ireland.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Renee D. Gala | President, CEO & Director | Age 53 | Compensation: $3.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $1.5M ranks in the top quartile among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 22%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $449K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $101K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Jazz Pharmaceuticals plc is a large-cap healthcare business with a $15.8B market cap on $4.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +5% over the past three years and +12% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size. Operating margins are contracting by -4.1pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 2% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $1.3B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 30 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, thin -1.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.8%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 3.0% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins contracting -4.1pp YoY \u2014 competitive pressure is eroding the franchise","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Operating margins 10% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.4% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $39.9M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 56/100): roic below cost of capital; leveraged balance sheet under pressure \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 68% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 41% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (25.6% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Jazz Pharmaceuticals CEO Touts Ziihera Launch, Pipeline After Raising Revenue Guidance","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/healthcare/articles/jazz-pharmaceuticals-ceo-touts-ziihera-121206402.html","date":"2026-11-21","timestamp":1795263126.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.361,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance","leadership","product"]},{"title":"Jazz Pharmaceuticals (JAZZ) Stock Looks Overvalued With A 90% Three Year Run","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/jazz-pharmaceuticals-jazz-stock-looks-051521655.html","date":"2026-11-21","timestamp":1795238121.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.915,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Should You Buy Jazz Pharmaceuticals Stock For Its Cash?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/buy-jazz-pharmaceuticals-stock-cash-152744275